<p><font face="helvetica,arial" size="4" color="000000"><b>IS THAT YOUR EPIC, OR ARE YOU JUST HAPPY TO SEE ME?</b></font></p>
<p align="justify"><font face="helvetica,arial" size="2" color="000000"><b>It wasn't long ago when the guild was shocked and amazed that Bobmd acquired
the guild's first epic, his Spear of Fate. Now, we are getting new epics to
guild members...four at a time? Yes, that's right; four Soldiers in one day
received their epics on Wednesday. Natakaz and Popajorgio finished Celestial
Fists (Xenevorash schmenevorash), Traban finished his Ragebringer at long
last, and Chamelius also acquired his spear.
<br><br>
<a href="images/ass2.jpg"><img align="left" width="200" height="150" src="images/ass2.gif"></a>Tuesday night was a powerful epic raid night; teamed with Tuatha de Dedann,
Soldiers plowed through <em>35</em> straight black reavers, 34 of which
spawned from the first, with what seemed like an endless domino effect of
corpse spawns. The entire guild was intrigued in guild chat for the
duration. Thanks to Tuatha also for helping Chamelius with the skywalk run
in City of Mist to drop Neh Ashir, and also offered to lead Annoly to the Wraith of Jaxion but she had ISP problems and went LD just before the venture up the sky ramp.
<br><br>
<a href="images/ass3.jpg"><img align="right" width="200" height="150" src="images/ass3.gif"></a>Chardok gave 42 determined Soldiers free ports to their bind points, but not before first dropping Prince Selrach Di'zok and taking his head, looted by
our beloved Chantci. The next trip will be solely for the Overking
Balthazid's Singed Scroll for one of those Water Sprinkler of Nem Ankhs all
the clerics are cheering about (something about 96% resurrection costing too
much mana). The revenge raid has been scheduled for Saturday, Sept. 21st, <a href="http://64.166.185.180/sod/raids.cfm">sign up here!</a>
<br><br>
<a href="images/ass4.jpg"><img align="left" width="200" height="150" src="images/ass4.gif"></a>Venril Sathir made the Soldiers' revenge list this week. After Transcended
had beat us to him, they wiped and let us have a shot while they ran
corpses. With a very well executed Rune V chain on Syrocco, we successfully
beat him down to 1% of his life, at which point Annoly ran out of mana and Venril got
the upper hand...repeatedly. After he dropped Syrocco with that supreme 1500
point lifetap, he then mowed through our very own Peter Pan (Zabooboo) and
the rest of the Soldiers quickly followed suit. Excellent fight, but not quite perfect, which is all the more
reason for mad revenge in the near future. Trans then proceeded to retort by
dropping Venril with more firepower than before. He dropped no wizard epic
piece; sorry Xetus, but don't worry...he'll get his.
<br><br>
<font face="arial" size="3"><b>Class Leaders --</b></font><br>
<a href="images/ass5.jpg"><img align="right" width="200" height="150" src="images/ass5.gif"></a>Soldiers have grown immensely over the past few months, and as such the
officers have decided to instate a class leader system to take care of epic
raid requests and progress tracking. While this is mostly to keep track of
epics, don't hesitate to ask class leaders for advice on your class,
class-related quests, or anything else. Be sure to check and participate on
the <a href="http://pub83.ezboard.com/bsoldiersofdestiny43227">forums</a>
for epic updates and the like in the class sections. Class leaders are
displayed in the messageboards. Be sure to check so you know who is yours!
<br><br>
<font face="arial" size="3"><b>Raids --</b></font><br>
There is a lot of action planned for the coming weeks. Be sure to visit the
<a href="http://64.166.185.180/sod/raids.cfm">raid page</a> for more details
and to sign ups. Also, Chuggette is not hosting weekly Umbral Plains
mini-raids to gear us up. Wednesday of each week a maximum of three full
groups will camp one of the various spots in Umbral for class armor. The
guidelines for this excellent idea are <a
href="http://pub83.ezboard.com/fsoldiersofdestiny43227frm10.showMessage?topi
cID=176.topic">here</a> (expect a full set of rules for these on the website
soon). This should definitely help everyone upgrade their armor, and fairly
fast. In addition to weekly Chugg's weekly Umbral raids, Shuruga is planning
weekly Kael raids for Sunday nights. Details on these raids can be found <a
href="http://pub83.ezboard.com/fsoldiersofdestiny43227frm10.showMessage?topi
cID=183.topic">here</a>. Good luck to everyone in those endeavors and I will
see you there I'm sure.
<br><br>
Vespina Meradin<br>
Teleporter de Mediocrity
<br><br>
Allies are welcome in the <a href="http://pub83.ezboard.com/bsoldiersofdestiny43227">forums</a> too! Enjoy =)
<br><br></b></font></p>

